{{also|indéclinable}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|indéclinable}}, from {{uder|en|frm|-}}, from {{der|en|la|indeclinabilis}}. See {{m|en|in-}} not, and {{m|en|decline}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# That one cannot [[decline]]; [[unavoidable]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1994|author=Helen R. Myers|title=To Wed at Christmas|page=101
|passage=He'd planned to work a double shift Friday night, but Gladys Silverman's '''indeclinable''' invitation threw a hefty wrench into David's plans.}}
# {{lb|en|grammar|of a word}} Not [[grammatically]] [[declinable]].

